FINAL VERIFICATION after all restores are proven. Foreground, standalone, unpiped. Read the OUTPUT, not the exit code: a `--filter` leg that prints no `Test Files N passed` count line ran nothing and is UNVERIFIED, and a `;`-chain reports only the last command's status — which is exactly why the stored command below wraps each leg in an `e` guard that exits on the first nonzero `$LASTEXITCODE`. Run the row's exact stored verification command VERBATIM and persist it verbatim as complete_task.verification.command:

& {$p='pnpm.exe';function e{if($LASTEXITCODE){exit $LASTEXITCODE}};foreach($f in 'src/live/live-keyed-session.test.ts','src/live/live-handshake.test.ts','src/scaffold.test.tsx','src/v2/cordum-app.test.tsx'){&$p --filter @moe/control-room exec vitest run $f;e};&$p exec vitest run tests/integration/control-room/pairing-claim-parity.test.ts;e;&$p --filter @moe/control-room typecheck;e;&$p --filter @moe/control-room test;e}

Architect ran it at HEAD aa828410, exit 0, every leg printing a nonzero count line: live-keyed-session.test.ts 1 file / 7 tests; live-handshake.test.ts 1 / 20; scaffold.test.tsx 1 / 37; cordum-app.test.tsx 1 / 34; pairing-claim-parity.test.ts 1 / 3 (root lane); `@moe/control-room typecheck` echoing `$ tsc --project tsconfig.json`; `@moe/control-room test` 113 files / 1543 tests. Require all seven again. If the host returns EINVAL on `pnpm.exe`, fall back to executable `pnpm` with the argv array preserved — never shell:true, never a piped or `;`-chained rewrite of this command. Also run `git diff --check --` the seven paths. Then rerun root `pnpm typecheck` and root `pnpm test`, compare failing-path sets against the step-1 baseline, and confirm the new-failure set intersected with the seven owned paths is EMPTY (it must be — this row changed no bytes). Disclose all foreign red verbatim with its exact failing lines and paths; never fabricate green.
